==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{term|ethnic}} + {{term|cleansing}}. Perhaps compare {{etyl|sh}} {{term|etničko čišćenje}}, though this is probably attested later. Originally used of (and still chiefly associated with) the wars in former Yugoslavia during the 1990s.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|sg=[[ethnic]] [[cleansing]]}}

# The [[mass]] [[extermination]] or [[expulsion]] of [[people]] belonging to one ethnic or [[religious]] [[group]] by those of another.

====Translations====
The cleansing translates as ethnic eradication of hoodrums. What occurred in Rwanda for example was religiuos ethnic cleasing.
The first religious ethnic cleasing of Islamist, Baptist and Roma is important. In 1994 Rwandan Interahamwe systematicaly killed
80,000 people who were of a different belief. It resulted in a cival war. The Rwanda army eventualy faught off U.N.peacekeepers
led by Nato Command to reestablish cival rule. The Belgian Para Commando and ISAF were expelled from Rwanda in 2011.

